{
  "boundary": "Single-GPU throughput on one rented 80 GiB H100 SXM, before grant access. It measures relative effects and anchors the plan's projections; it does not qualify GH200, distributed execution, scheduler requeue, long-context cost or data eligibility, and freezes no immutable setting. GH200 carries the same Hopper GPU with more memory and more bandwidth, so for this bandwidth-bound workload its rates should be at or above these.",
  "command": "From the clean bundled code checkout after `scripts.gh200_check bind ..`, run `python experiments/qualification/check_throughput_packet.py experiments/qualification/throughput-h100.json --print-commands`. Substitute selected geometry in the copied commands, preserving tokens per update; do not edit the tracked packet during measurement. Printed selected values are preflight probes, not measured selections.",
  "common": {
    "activation_checkpointing": false,
    "compile_mode": "max-autotune-no-cudagraphs",
    "deterministic": true,
    "experiment": "../relocated-base",
    "loss_backend": "liger",
    "mode": "compute",
    "peak_tflops": 989.5,
    "sequence_length": 4096,
    "steps": 30,
    "warmup_steps": 10,
    "output_directory": "../results/throughput-h100",
    "data_dir": "../pilot-data",
    "data_dir_note": "Relative to the bundled code/ checkout after binding. Only end-to-end mode reads the transported pilot-data/ pack; compute mode is synthetic."
  },
  "date": "2026-09-26",
  "decisions_to_record": [
    "Parent tokens per second and model FLOPs utilization at each microbatch, and the speedup over the pilot recipe on the same host.",
    "The fastest microbatch that fits 80 GiB, for the parent and each rung. It is a candidate only: device_batch_size is frozen on GH200.",
    "Whether liger_aligned is faster than liger by more than the noise band, at the parent and at each rung. It fails restart parity (see speck/model/layers.py), so a gain only decides whether finding that cause is worth the work.",
    "Tokens per second per rung, which replaces the plan's 25% utilization assumption when the budget lines are converted into run counts.",
    "Whether the KDA custom-op work is worth funding, judged from the Hopper profile."
  ],
  "estimated_gpu_hours": 8,
  "format": "speck_h100_throughput_rental",
  "format_version": 1,
  "input_receipts": {
    "experiments/qualification/throughput-3090/sweep.json": "56b1fce0fd067792585a950014d64d8f5610a83c2e6fe05ffaf957f622d8dddf"
  },
  "out_of_scope": [
    "Compiled execution under DistributedDataParallel. This sweep is single-GPU, and base.py compiles the DDP-wrapped module with six graph breaks still present. Qualify it separately with `scripts.training_replay --compile --workers 4` before any compiled production wave.",
    "max-autotune warmup cost, which the thirty-step measurement excludes. Amortize it per wave using the persistent TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR the Slurm renderer exports."
  ],
  "parent_speedup_status": "unmeasured_before_this_sweep: no parent configuration with activation checkpointing off was ever measured, because two attempts reached 23.03 and 22.91 GiB before exhausting the 24 GiB card.",
  "prerequisites": [
    "Confirm the card is an 80 GiB H100 SXM before spending anything.",
    "Run `scripts.gh200_check run --allow-other-gpu` first, so the single-worker path is known to work on this host.",
    "Export a persistent TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR so max-autotune compiles once, not per run.",
    "Record SM clock, temperature and power; reject any result whose clock moved beyond 5%.",
    "Establish the noise band from the five h100-mb4 runs before reading any delta."
  ],
  "purpose": "Measure the 1.2B parent's and every ladder rung's throughput and utilization on Hopper before grant access, and settle the liger_aligned loss A/B, so the budget lines become run counts from measurements instead of an assumed 25% utilization.",
